-- title:
--   Norm group of an exponent-p extension unramified outside S
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a number field, $p$ a prime, and suppose $E$ contains an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes with $p \in S$. Then there exist a number field $F$ and an $E$-algebra structure on $F$ making $F/E$ Galois such that: the group $F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} F$ of $E$-automorphisms of $F$ is commutative and every one of its elements satisfies $\sigma^p = 1$; for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_F$ that does not lie above any prime of $S$ (that is, for which no rational prime in $S$ lies in $w$), the ramification index `Ideal.ramificationIdx'` of $w$ over the prime of $\mathcal{O}_E$ underlying it equals $1$; and, inside the unit group of the adèle ring of $E$, the subgroup generated by the principal idèles (the image of $E^\times$ under the map induced by $E \to \mathbb{A}_E$) together with the image of the idelic norm of the canonical base change `genuineBaseChange E F` (the units map applied to the algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_F \to \mathbb{A}_E$ for the canonical ring homomorphism $\mathbb{A}_E \to \mathbb{A}_F$, which is compatible with $E \to F$ and induces $\mathbb{A}_E \otimes_E F \cong \mathbb{A}_F$) coincides with the subgroup generated by the principal idèles, the $p$-th powers of idèle units, and `unitIdelesTrivialOn` for the set of finite places of $E$ above $S$, namely those idèle units whose archimedean part is $1$, whose component at each place above $S$ is $1$, and which together with their inverse are integral at every finite place not above $S$.
--
--   This is the existence theorem of global class field theory at $p$ with ramification restricted to $S$, in norm-group form: classically $F$ is the Kummer extension $E(V_S^{1/p})$, the maximal abelian extension of exponent $p$ unramified outside $S$, and the displayed identity identifies its norm group as $E^\times \cdot \mathbb{I}_E^p \cdot U_E^S$. It feeds the computation of the action on $S$-class groups in [`M4aHerbrand.exists_isGalois_forall_prod_sClassAct_eq_pow_of_isPrimitiveRoot`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_isGalois_forall_prod_sClassAct_eq_pow_of_isPrimitiveRoot).
